All three queries reach the same numeric result, but 2result.sql is the most robust:

• It isolates Yash Chopra’s PID once in a dedicated CTE (yash_pid), avoiding repeated sub‑queries or possible duplication.  
• Every PID taken from the relationship tables is uniformly TRIM‑med, eliminating leading‑space anomalies that otherwise create separate, duplicate IDs.  
• Collaborations with “other” directors are gathered in one pass (pair_counts) and then re‑used for both the Yash‑film count and the MAX‑with‑others computation, keeping the logic compact and avoiding double counting.  

Because it is both concise and handles the data‑cleanliness issues explicitly, it is the safest choice.

